--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT licence above covers the contents of this repository: the Dockerfile,
the shell scripts and the documentation.

It does not, and cannot, relicense anything those files download. This
repository bundles no third-party code — every component is fetched from its
own upstream at build or run time and keeps its own licence:

  Wine                                    LGPL-2.1-or-later
  DXVK                                    Zlib
  vkd3d-proton                            LGPL-2.1-or-later
  AffinityPluginLoader                    MIT
  WineFix (APL plugin)                    GPL-2.0
  d2d1.dll bundled with WineFix           LGPL-2.1
  Microsoft .NET Framework 4.8            proprietary, Microsoft redistributable
  Microsoft Visual C++ runtime            proprietary, Microsoft redistributable

A built image therefore contains software under several licences placed side by
side. That is mere aggregation, not a combined work: these scripts install and
invoke those components, they do not link against or derive from them.

Affinity itself is proprietary software belonging to Canva. It is downloaded
from the vendor at first run, under the vendor's own terms, and is neither
included in this repository nor redistributed by it. You need whatever licence
or account Canva requires in order to use it.
